Well, someone said that we might as well "pick one in 500 starting
characters and let them win immediately", and Toby talks about first
time players who "just got lucky". He wants to force these YAFAP
players to do things his way, in order to prevent disappointment. (For
them, presumably.) Greg makes the point that the game seems hard
enough already -- to him, to me, and to the vast majority of people on
Earth. So it seems to me, anyway. I haven't seen this "disappointment"
in new players, and I have met with puzzlement when I tell people I
avoid save-scumming. Most people seem to view a game that can kill
your character instantly, with no saving in the expected sense of the
word, as difficult enough. An early wand decreases the difficulty, but
not enough to destroy all the fun or challenge for inexperienced
players like us. So, Toby, your worries seem misplaced.

> The question is whether it let you ascend when you were not in fact
