implication for the sake of argument. If the logic of the game allows
one to win with a bit less sacrifice (in terms of time, health and the
real world in general), so what? They still had to spent effort on it.
Heck, one mistake with a (BoH could've destroyed their advantage. What
justifies forcing an unwanted conduct on them, even an "easy" conduct?
 
